-- title:
--   Gotzmann freeness step over a local base
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $n$, $m$, $g$ and a commutative local ring $A$, and let $F : \mathrm{Fin}\,g \to A[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ be a family of polynomials in $n+1$ variables with each $F_i$ homogeneous of degree $m$. Write $I = (F_0,\dots,F_{g-1})$ for the ideal generated by the range of $F$, and for a degree $d$ let `piece I d` be the $A$-module quotient of the $A$-submodule $A[x]_d$ of forms of degree $d$ by the submodule of those forms that lie in $I$. Assume that `piece I m` and `piece I (m+1)` are projective $A$-modules, and assume the following condition on relations over the residue field $k = A/\mathfrak m$: for every $d$ and every tuple $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,g \to k[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ with all $c_i$ homogeneous of degree $d$ and $\sum_i c_i \bar F_i = 0$, where $\bar F_i$ denotes the coefficientwise reduction of $F_i$ along the residue map, the tuple $c$ lies in the $k[x]$-submodule of $k[x]^g$ spanned by those tuples $l$ for which there is some $d' \le 1$ with every $l_i$ homogeneous of degree $d'$ and $\sum_i l_i \bar F_i = 0$. The conclusion is that for every $e$ the $A$-module `piece I e` is free.
--
--   This is the passage from the closed fibre to an arbitrary local base in Gotzmann's flatness criterion, isolated as a statement of commutative algebra: no Noetherian hypothesis and no Hilbert-polynomial count enter. It is used in the construction of Hilbert functors, via [`AlgebraicGeometry.HilbertFunctor.exists_point_I_eq_of_projective_piece_succ`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.HilbertFunctor.exists_point_I_eq_of_projective_piece_succ), and rests on the local freeness criterion [`Module.free_quotient_range_of_ker_baseChange_residueField_le`](thm.html#Module.free_quotient_range_of_ker_baseChange_residueField_le) applied to the presentation maps $A[x]_d^g \to A[x]_{m+d}$, $(a_i) \mapsto \sum_i a_i F_i$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_HilbertFunctor_free_piece_of_isLocalRing_of_forall_relation_mem_span.lean

